---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The jumping rope — León Palafox"
  description="An interactive picture of regression uncertainty: a rope pinned at the observations thrashes where the data leaves it free, and settles as points are added."
>
  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-14 sm:px-10 lg:px-14 lg:py-20">
    <p class="micro-label flex items-center gap-3 text-signal-deep">
      <span>Interactive</span>
      <span lang="ja" class="tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">縄跳び</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
      The jumping rope
    </h1>
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-6 block h-[3px] w-14 bg-signal"></span>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Regression is a rope held at the points you have measured. Where observations are close together the rope is
      pinned and barely moves. Where they are far apart it thrashes — and that thrashing <em>is</em> the uncertainty in
      your predictions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-12 sm:px-10 lg:px-14">
    <div
      data-rope
      class="mx-auto max-w-5xl"
      role="group"
      aria-label="Interactive regression uncertainty visualisation"
    >
      <div class="relative aspect-[16/10] w-full border border-hairline bg-paper sm:aspect-[16/9]">
        <canvas data-rope-canvas class="block size-full cursor-crosshair touch-manipulation"></canvas>

        <p class="micro-label pointer-events-none absolute bottom-3 left-4 text-muted">Click the panel to pin a point</p>

        <div class="pointer-events-none absolute right-4 top-3 text-right">
          <p class="micro-label text-muted">Slack in the rope</p>
          <p data-rope-readout class="mt-1 font-mono text-2xl leading-none text-signal-deep" aria-live="polite">±0.00</p>
          <p class="micro-label mt-2 text-muted">
            <span data-rope-count>2</span> observations
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <noscript>
        <p class="mt-4 border border-hairline bg-paper p-4 text-sm text-muted">
          This visualisation needs JavaScript. The short version: with two observations the fitted curve is almost
          unconstrained between them and swings wildly; each new observation shortens the leash until the curve barely
          moves at all.
        </p>
      </noscript>

      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <button
            data-rope-add
            type="button"
            class="micro-label border border-ink bg-ink px-3 py-2 text-paper transition-colors hover:bg-signal-deep hover:border-signal-deep"
          >
            Add observation
          </button>
          <button
            data-rope-undo
            type="button"
            class="micro-label border border-hairline px-3 py-2 transition-colors hover:border-ink"
          >
            Undo
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          <button
            data-rope-reset
            type="button"
            class="micro-label border border-hairline px-3 py-2 transition-colors hover:border-ink"
          >
            Reset
          </button>
          <button
            data-rope-play
            type="button"
            aria-pressed="true"
            class="micro-label border border-hairline px-3 py-2 transition-colors hover:border-ink"
          >
            Pause
          </button>
        </div>

        <label class="block">
          <span class="micro-label text-muted">Rope stiffness</span>
          <input
            data-rope-stiffness
            type="range"
            min="0.18"
            max="1.1"
            step="0.01"
            value="0.45"
            class="mt-2 w-full accent-[#e2371b]"
          />
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">How hard the rope resists bending between pins.</span>
        </label>

        <label class="block">
          <span class="micro-label text-muted">Pin tightness</span>
          <input
            data-rope-tightness
            type="range"
            min="0.02"
            max="0.3"
            step="0.005"
            value="0.05"
            class="mt-2 w-full accent-[#e2371b]"
          />
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">How firmly each observation holds the rope down.</span>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-hairline px-6 py-14 sm:px-10 lg:px-14">
    <SectionHeading title="What you are looking at" />
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label text-signal-deep">The ropes</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Seven red strands, each a curve that is fully consistent with the observations. They are not decoration: every
          frame is an honest draw from the posterior, so wherever the strands separate, the data genuinely does not say
          which one is right.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label text-signal-deep">The band</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The ±2σ envelope — the region the rope stays inside about 95% of the time. Watch it pinch shut at each pin and
          balloon in the gaps. The number in the corner is its average width, which is the one-line summary of how much
          you still do not know.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="micro-label text-signal-deep">The dark line</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The posterior mean — the single curve a normal regression would hand you. It is the least interesting object on
          the screen. Reporting it alone is exactly the habit this picture is meant to break.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-14 sm:px-10 lg:px-14">
    <SectionHeading title="Things worth trying" />
    <ul class="mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.6em] size-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-signal"></span>
        <span>
          Reset to two points and watch the middle. The rope is pinned at both ends and still swings almost as freely as
          if you had measured nothing at all: at the midpoint those two observations close the band by under a tenth.
          Two points say very little about what happens between them.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.6em] size-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-signal"></span>
        <span>
          Add points one at a time and watch the slack number fall. It drops fast and then barely at all: averaged over
          many runs, the fifth observation buys about thirty times as much certainty as the twentieth. Most of what a
          dataset can tell you arrives early.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.6em] size-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-signal"></span>
        <span>
          Pin several points close together on one side, then look at the far side. Clustered data collapses uncertainty
          locally and does almost nothing for the region you never measured. This is what extrapolation costs.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.6em] size-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-signal"></span>
        <span>
          Now push stiffness up without touching the data. The slack collapses — on a fixed set of four points it runs
          from about ±0.43 at the loosest setting to ±0.05 at the stiffest. You did not measure anything to earn that.
          A stiff rope is just a strong prior that the truth is smooth, and if it is not, the narrow band is false
          confidence. Note the rope stays curved throughout: stiffness buys smoothness, never straightness.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <a
      href="/teaching/"
      class="group micro-label mt-12 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-signal-deep hover:text-signal"
    >
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-1">←</span>
      Teaching
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import { mountRopeScene } from '../../scripts/rope-scene';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rope]');
  if (root) mountRopeScene(root);
</script>
